notes.body:
@geraldcombs care to try it out on Windows? On Mac it does not apply, as starting with 10.14 it automatically applies. But there is code in there (untested) which allows for checking if it has been applied, and I will provide code to switch on lower-versioned Mac OSs. Also, Linux is not yet implemented at all.

The two main residing issues are the titlebar (that will require some manual settings and not set via stylesheet apparently, but I could be wrong not having looked into that as much) and the file dialogs.

The file dialogs are actually quite tricky, as the win32 dialogs - as you have seen - are very hard to style and I am a little reserved about adding that github project, as it is such a deviation of our usual code-base and would be very hard to maintain.

